# CHRONOVOLT CASE — Open Hardware Spec v1.0
### Kinetic-Charging Phone Case // Self-Winding Clockwork meets Piezo-Hybrid Harvest
**Status: OPEN SOURCE. Take it, build it, sell it, remix it. No permission required. No credit required (but a nod is cool).**
BEKW-CODE public release — EK'VESH'ARUN·7777·KAN

---

## 1. CONCEPT SUMMARY

A rugged, clear-shell phone case with a visible internal clockwork mechanism. A flush-mounted spin dial on the case back acts as the manual input — flick it like a coin and it free-spins on a low-friction bearing for minutes, slowly fceeding a step-up gear train that drives a micro electromagnetic generator (primary power) and a piezo ceramic ring (secondary harvest + visual/tactile pulse). Output trickle-charges the phone via a buffered supercapacitor/thin LiPo cell.

Passive ambient charging also occurs from walking/arm motion via an off-center weighted rotor, same principle as a self-winding watch.

**Design ethos:** durable like a rugged case, beautiful like an exposed watch movement, honest about what it actually does (trickle/extender power, not primary fast-charging).

---

## 2. MECHANICAL SYSTEM

### 2.1 Spin Dial (manual input)
- Flush-mounted circular dial on case back, finger-flickable, no folding parts.
- Sealed low-friction bearing core (ceramic or stainless ball bearing) — minimizes drag for long spin-down (target: 90–180 seconds per flick at moderate force).
- Tungsten or brass weights embedded at rim — flywheel effect, increases angular momentum and spin-down time.
- Textured grip ring at outer edge for thumb traction.
- One-way sprag clutch / ratchet engages step-up gear train in drive direction only — dial free-spins independent of load, only "bites" the gear train rotationally (same principle as automatic watch rotor pawls).

### 2.2 Passive Ambient Rotor
- Off-center semicircular weighted rotor (brass or tungsten), same general principle as automatic watch movements.
- Driven by arm/body motion during normal carry and use.
- Engages the same step-up gear train via a separate one-way gear path, merged at a differential or simple OR-gate freewheel junction so either input source can drive the train without backdriving the other.

### 2.3 Step-Up Gear Train
- Multi-stage gear train, ~1:50 to 1:80 ratio (tunable), converts low-RPM hand/body input into high-RPM generator input.
- Brass or polymer (POM/Delrin) gears for low friction, low cost, quiet operation.
- Fully visible through clear shell window — this is the centerpiece visual.

### 2.4 Housing / Durability
- Outer shell: clear polycarbonate (PC), tinted-clear or full-clear.
- Internal shock-isolation pod: gear train and generator assembly mounted on a separate TPU-dampened internal frame, isolated from direct impact transfer (drop-tested independent of shell flex).
- Bumper layer: TPU corner/edge bumper, standard rugged-case configuration.
- Target drop rating: MIL-STD-810G, 6 ft (1.8m) onto concrete, multi-orientation.
- Sealed gear compartment: dust/splash resistant (IP54 target), not full submersion.

---

## 3. ELECTRICAL SYSTEM

### 3.1 Generation
| Component | Role | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| Micro electromagnetic coil + NdFeB magnet rotor | Primary generation | Same family as shake-flashlight generators; efficient at low RPM |
| Piezoelectric ceramic ring (PZT discs) | Secondary harvest + pulse trigger | Struck/flexed at gear mesh points; low energy density but drives the LED pulse and senses motion |

### 3.2 Power Conditioning
- Rectifier (full-wave bridge, low-VF Schottky diodes)
- Voltage regulator / power management IC (buck-boost, low quiescent draw)
- Buffer storage: supercapacitor (1–3F) for fast charge/discharge cycling, OR thin-format LiPo cell (150–300mAh) for smoother sustained output — supercap recommended for durability/cycle-life, since this will be charged/discharged thousands of times.

### 3.3 Output
- USB-C output port (PD-aware trickle, 5V/0.5A typical) OR Qi-style inductive pad on inner case face for direct phone contact charging.
- Status LED: pulses with each piezo strike (visual feedback — this is also the "mesmerizing" element, ties light to mechanical motion in real time).

### 3.4 Realistic Output Expectations (be honest in all marketing/specs)
- One vigorous flick (spin-down ~2 min): rough estimate 0.3–0.8 Wh harvested depending on final generator efficiency — order of magnitude similar to small hand-crank flashlight generators.
- This is **extender/emergency power**, not a replacement for wall charging. Position it that way. The mechanism is the product; the charge is a legitimate bonus, not a hoax claim.

